GCD :
The Greatest Common Divisor (GCD) of two numbers is the largest number that divides both of them completely.

Examples:

GCD(12, 18) = 6

GCD(14, 28) = 14

GCD(8, 9) = 1 (co-prime numbers)

Java Program – Brute Force Method

Check all numbers from 1 to min(a, b) and find the largest divisor.

import java.util.Scanner;

public class GCD_BruteForce {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        // Input numbers
        System.out.print("Enter first number: ");
        int a = sc.nextInt();
        System.out.print("Enter second number: ");
        int b = sc.nextInt();

        int gcd = 1;
//We start with gcd = 1 because 1 is always a divisor of any number.
//This variable will store the largest number that divides both a and b.

        // Brute force: check all numbers up to min(a, b)
        for (int i = 1; i <= Math.min(a, b); i++) {
            if (a % i == 0 && b % i == 0) {
                gcd = i;
            }
        }

        System.out.println("GCD of " + a + " and " + b + " is: " + gcd);

        sc.close();
    }
}
Java Program – Euclidean Algorithm (Efficient)
import java.util.Scanner;

public class GCD_Euclidean {
    public static int gcd(int a, int b) {
        // Euclidean algorithm
        while (b != 0) {
            int temp = b;
            b = a % b;
            a = temp;
        }
        return a;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        // Input numbers
        System.out.print("Enter first number: ");
        int a = sc.nextInt();
        System.out.print("Enter second number: ");
        int b = sc.nextInt();

        System.out.println("GCD of " + a + " and " + b + " is: " + gcd(a, b));

        sc.close();
    }
}
Enter first number: 48
Enter second number: 18
GCD of 48 and 18 is: 6

🔹 Solution With temp

That’s why we store the old b in temp before changing b:

int temp = b;   // save original b
b = a % b;      // calculate remainder
a = temp;       // now assign original b into a


This correctly implements the formula:

new a = old b

new b = old a % old b

🔹 Example (48, 18)

Step 1:

temp = 18

b = 48 % 18 = 12

a = 18

Now pair becomes (18, 12) ✅ which matches GCD(48, 18) = GCD(18, 12)

